    <main class="container">
        <div class="grid-full-page">
            <div>
                <div class="full-width-card">
                    <h2>Definition of Problematic Social Media Use</h2>
                    <p>Problematic social media use refers to excessive, compulsive engagement with platforms that interferes with daily life, sleep schedules, academic focus, and psychological well-being.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="full-width-card">
                    <h2>"Scrolling Out Lives Away" Explanations</h2>
                    <p>Endless algorithmic feeds exploit human dopamine pathways, trapping users in passive consumption loops where hours pass unnoticed at the expense of meaningful real-world activities.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="full-width-card">
                    <h2>Facts and Opinions</h2>
                    <p>Research confirms a strong correlation between high screen time and increased anxiety, whereas popular debates often oversimplify complex mental health factors into singular tech blame.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="full-width-card">
                    <h2>Summary</h2>
                    <p>Recognizing the mechanics of algorithmic retention is the first step toward establishing healthy digital boundaries and purposeful online usage.</p>
                    <div class="citation-box">
                        <strong>Sources Cited:</strong> Netsafe NZ Algorithms Report; Mental Health Foundation of New Zealand.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <aside class="visual-sidebar">
                <img src="/static/images/engagement.png" alt="Social Media Algorithm Engagement Rates">
